h Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:38b975f24a2e7e6f69","definition":"To protect from danger; to secure against surprise, attack, or injury; to keep in safety; to defend.","example":"All of the mountain passes are guarded by troops.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["foreguard","fox guarding the henhouse","guardable","guardage","guardee","guardingly","guarding post","guard one's tongue","unguard","wolf guarding the sheep"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b62a31440a5b735068","definition":"To keep watch over, in order to prevent escape or restrain from acts of violence, or the like.","example":"Guard the prisoner.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["foreguard","fox guarding the henhouse","guardable","guardage","guardee","guardingly","guarding post","guard one's tongue","unguard","wolf guarding the sheep"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ed689a64ddfb9e32b9","definition":"To watch by way of caution or defense; to be cautious; to be in a state or position of defense or safety.","example":"Careful people guard against mistakes.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":["foreguard","fox guarding the henhouse","guardable","guardage","guardee","guardingly","guarding post","guard one's tongue","unguard","wolf guarding the sheep"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en